  "title": "Notification of Solution doesn't tell me it's mine",
  "content": "<p>We’ve already noted the pointless notifications on a user’s own actions:</p><p><a href=\"https://community.st.com/feedback-forum-118/don-t-notify-me-about-my-comment-166763\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow ugc\" target=\"_self\">https://community.st.com/feedback%2Dforum%2D118/don%2Dt%2Dnotify%2Dme%2Dabout%2Dmy%2Dcomment%2D166763</a></p><oembed url=\"https://community.st.com/feedback-forum-118/unnecessary-notifications-166172\"></oembed><p> </p><p>But the ‘Best Answer’ notification doesn’t identify when it’s my answer that was chosen:</p><figure><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://uploads-eu-west-1.insided.com/stmicroelectronics-en/attachment/30b28ff0-d8b0-4a65-993f-72bd6a156bb9.png\" /></figure><p> </p><p>The old forum did used to distinguish “<em><strong>an</strong></em> answer has been marked” - ie, somebody else’s answer - from “<em><strong>your</strong></em> answer has been marked”</p>",
